# The absolute value of a 2-limb number: its negation when the leading limb is negative, which for
# a normalized number is when the number is.
kernel:        abs_2
input:         x = x0 x1
output:        z = z0 z1
value:         abs(x)
requires:      normalized x
ensures:       normalized z
ensures:       error z R c=0 k=2 t=0
source:        the sign of x0 (Milestone 1 listing)
status:        unverified
cone_exempt:   the limbs reach the outputs through select; each output limb is an input limb up to sign, so it is non-finite exactly when that input limb is, and the non-finite layer tests the operand

m  = lt(x0, 0)
n0 = neg(x0)
n1 = neg(x1)
z0 = select(m, n0, x0)
z1 = select(m, n1, x1)
